; profile: step=one
; Two firings that select different rows yet do not commute: the rows share
; an unknown, and each rule tells it a different value (the SharedUnknown
; control of JointFirings/Independent).  After either, the other is refused,
; so each order is an outcome of its own.  Negative example for the lookup of
; independent firings, which needs states of fixed terms.
(left $x)
(right $x)
(rule five (take (left $v)) (tell (= $v 5)) (make (five $v)))
(rule six (take (right $v)) (tell (= $v 6)) (make (six $v)))
